Conditional Edge

A conditional edge chooses the next node based on some condition.

Instead of one road, there are multiple possible roads.

Flow
               Yes
              /
Planner -----> Researcher
     \
      \
       No
        \
         Writer

The graph decides where to go.

Example

Suppose your chatbot checks whether the user asked a question about products.

If Product Question

User
   |
Planner
   |
Product Agent
   |
END

If General Question

User
   |
Planner
   |
General Agent
   |
END

=======

Python Example
def router(state):

    if state["type"] == "product":
        return "product_agent"

    else:
        return "general_agent"

Add conditional edge

graph.add_conditional_edges(
    "planner",
    router,
    {
        "product_agent": "product_agent",
        "general_agent": "general_agent",
    }
)

